WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:36.850
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.420
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.940
In the Rock Wasteland, a mysterious monster appeared before me.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.780
Is it an ancient soldier who destroyed Atlantis?

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:48.890
Chris and Ironheart are the souls of warriors who allied with Duel Monsters to fight them.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.540
I promise to fight for those who helped me!

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:01.900
Valon on the Move!
Mysterious Armor Deck

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.240
Finally, we're back on the tracks.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.140
Yeah.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.860
If we follow the tracks, we'll meet up with Jonouchi.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.800
I want to tell Jonouchi right away.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.170
That Yugi is fine.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.520
That he's back to his normal self!

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.090
Let's go.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.020
Yeah.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.160
198...

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.380
199...

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.080
200.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.790
I can't move.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.130
C'mon.  One-Two-Shoot!

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.710
You punk!  That's not fair!

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.960
You know I'm in a daze!

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.150
Be quiet!  A win's a win!

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.170
You're carrying Ryuzaki.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.960
I need a rest.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.920
Are you sure?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.170
Didn't something happen to Yugi?

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.180
Oh, that's right.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.640
Let's go, Honda!

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.970
Don't you think we should rest first?

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.180
Jonouchi!

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.640
Pace yourself!

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.690
I didn't order you to do that.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.480
Order?  Listen up!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.830
I don't duel because someone orders me to!

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:45.170
I fought Pegasus and Jonouchi with my own free will!

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.400
Watch your tongue, Mai Kujaku.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.450
But you couldn't defeat Jonouchi.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.980
Stop joking around!

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.280
I would've won if he didn't stop me!

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.780
Still saying that?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.210
I do what I want to do.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:06.140
Dartz!  I won't even let you interfere in my duel!

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.500
Let her be.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:21.740
Her destiny is already in our god's hands.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.970
Jonouchi...

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.350
Hey girl.  That's an awesome bike.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.580
Come play with us.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.350
Get lost.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.590
What did you say?

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.240
I said, “Get lost!”

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.920
What'll you do with that toy?

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.940
No way!  It's not a hologram?

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.220
Valon?

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.940
I'll take care of Jonouchi.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.020
It's none of your business.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.800
I'm doing it for you.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.530
I'll defeat Jonouchi for you.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.530
For me?  Don't be ridiculous.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.270
You and I are the same.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.270
The same?  What do you mean?

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:38.270
It's in your eyes.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:46.060
You said you clung on to victory so that you can be free from the agony of losing.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.110
But that's not all.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.260
You hungered for victory.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.260
Your hunger drove you.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.760
I hungered for victory?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:06.270
Yes.  Like a vampire thirsting for blood, you thirsted for victory.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:11.270
But even a victory won't satisfy your hunger.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.950
You'll hunger for another victory.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.960
Ridiculous!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.620
You don't know what you're talking about!

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.320
Know why I know?

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.440
You don't have a cause.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.720
No matter how many times you win, you have nothing to win for.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:42.300
Jonouchi and the Pharaoh do.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.980
Rafael and Amelda also have their reasons.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.980
So do I, Mai.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.610
I had to keep winning to live.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.980
But I finally found a reason to win.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:58.560
It's you, Mai.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:04.350
Mai.  Be mine.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.630
I'll keep winning for you.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.600
I'll defeat Jonouchi and the Pharaoh.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.000
If you want, I'll even defeat Dartz!

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:19.010
And can you defeat me?

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.040
I've already-

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.170
I've changed since then!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:27.750
You shouldn't say that you'll keep winning easily.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.750
Mai.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.670
Is the professor okay?

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.630
He's a bit tired.  He's sleeping.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.900
He hasn't recovered from his shock and fatigue.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.410
Yeah.  But he wanted to get going.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.110
That's Mai!

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.190
And he's...

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.160
He's Doma!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:26.910
Becky!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.680
Otogi?

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:36.920
You took Yugi's soul!

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.920
So what?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.540
It's unforgivable!

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.420
And?

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.060
I'll defeat you!

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:46.660
Let's battle!

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.000
Wait, Becky!  It's too dangerous!

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:53.170
Don't underestimate me!  I'm the American champ!

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:57.440
I'll defeat him and get Yugi's soul back!

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.910
A little girl like you?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.410
American champ, Rebecca Hopkins.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:06.350
If you underestimate me, you'll pay!

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.140
How precocious.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:13.710
Defeating a kid will bother my conscience.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.360
But Mai, I'll show you a bit of my skills.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.360
I'll duel you, young lady.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.240
Becky, I'll duel too!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.370
I can help a little!

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.260
Fine.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:31.490
I'll take you both on at once!  Bring it!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.560
Becky!  Watch out for The Seal of Orichalcos!

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:40.380
Right!

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:43.390
Duel!

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.050
I'll go first.  Here I go!

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:15.050
I draw!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:19.260
I summon Psychic Armor Head in attack position!

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:24.800
He summoned a monster with 0 attack points in attack position?

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.860
Psychic Armor Head?

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.650
I've never seen that card.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.800
What can it do?

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:33.080
I end my turn.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.300
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:40.580
From my hand, I activate the spell card, Summon Dice!

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:44.000
I pay 1000 life points to roll a die!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:52.590
If I roll a 1 or 2, I can summon twice this turn.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:58.330
If I roll a 3 or 4, I can Special Summon a monster from the graveyard.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.060
And if I roll a 5 or 6...

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:05.860
It's 6!

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:09.870
I can summon a high-Level monster without tributing!

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.810
Come, Orgoth the Relentless!

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.310
I end my turn!

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:21.730
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:25.600
I summon Luster Dragon in attack position!

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:31.330
Next, I set a card.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.560
I end my turn!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.860
He can attack next turn.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.300
What'll he do?

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:42.800
My turn!

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:45.680
I activate Psychic Armor Head's effect!

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:53.120
Instead of drawing this turn, I add an Armor Monster from my deck to my hand.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:13:01.190
I tribute Psychic Armor Head to summon Double Cloth Armor!

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:13.570
I set a card and end my turn.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.250
What's he thinking?

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.710
He summoned another monster with 0 attack points.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:24.840
I'll let you know that this monster can't attack on my turn.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:30.800
But when it's attacked, its effect destroys your monster.

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:35.220
And you take damage equal to half its attack points.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:39.460
And this card is destroyed after the battle.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:43.220
I see!  If I attack with Orgoth the Relentless...

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:48.470
...I lose 250 life points, which is half its attack points.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:53.470
But he'll have no monsters on his next turn.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.030
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.380
I set a card!

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:01.350
The rest is up to you, Becky.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:07.990
Orgoth the Relentless, attack Double Cloth Armor!

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.360
Destroy it!  Diamond Blade!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.540
Now, Becky!

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:27.770
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.480
I set a card.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:35.450
I tribute Luster Dragon to summon Luster Dragon #2!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:44.790
Luster Dragon #2 attacks you directly!

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.800
I flip over my set card!

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.300
Magnet Armor!

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:57.880
It Special Summons an Armor Monster from my graveyard in attack position.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:02.080
I summon Double Cloth Armor!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.110
What?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.970
It's not over.  I activate my trap card!

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.470
Rope of Life!

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:36.480
When a battle sends a monster to the graveyard...

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:39.210
...I can discard my entire hand.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:45.790
That lets me Special Summon the monster with 800 extra attack points!

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:51.230
That's not all!  My Quick-Play Spell!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.060
Adamantine Sword Revival!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:59.500
It activates when a Dragon is Special Summoned from the graveyard.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:08.170
I tribute it to Special Summon Diamond Head Dragon on the owner's field in attack position!

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.490
Take it, Becky!

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:30.230
Diamond Head Dragon's attack points are equal to the tributed Dragon's attack points plus 1000!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.000
Thank you, Otogi!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.250
How's that!  I end my turn.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.740
W-What?

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.740
You had your fun.

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:46.330
But I'm done playing with you.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:47.650
My turn!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.020
I draw!

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:06.170
Psychic Armor Head has another effect.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:12.140
When it's in the graveyard, I can Special Summon it during the Standby Phase in attack position.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:16.940
Mai, I'll show you a bit of my skills.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:24.680
Are you planning to use The Seal of Orichalcos?

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.830
Don't flatter yourself.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:31.230
I don't need to use The Seal of Orichalcos against you.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:32.420
Here I go!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.190
My spell card!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.700
Armored Gravitation!

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:08.630
What?

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:12.200
The player equips the armor?

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:18.540
When Big Bang Blow is destroyed in battle...

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.320
...all monsters on the field are destroyed.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:26.580
And we both take damage equal to the destroyed monsters' attack points.

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:30.450
What?  If you do that, you'll lose too!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.930
Wanna put that to the test?

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.660
This is the end!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.890
I activate my trap card!

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.200
Mirror Force!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.670
It won't work!

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.540
No way!

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:56.440
The End Of Crusher!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:28.560
No way...

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:30.310
Why?

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:37.820
Tell Jonouchi that he's next.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.160
Mai...

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:59.220
Honda!  You cheater!

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:02.200
You made me carry Ryuzaki for 5000 steps!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.510
Be quiet!  You're the one who ran off!

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:12.250
Hey, Honda.  Look.

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:15.490
What?  An aurora?

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:24.590
We saw an aurora last time too.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:27.070
Yeah.  It's the same as before.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:40.010
Is something about to happen?

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:48.170
It's almost time.

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:53.020
My god is starting to move, hungry for powerful souls.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.700
Big brother, is it true?

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:09.770
I still can't believe Yugi lost.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:14.000
It means that even he has a ceiling.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.780
I have no business with losers.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.850
Big brother, look!  An aurora!

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:24.820
Aurora?

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.830
It's beautiful!

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:34.800
Why is there an aurora here?

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:39.800
There's a low pressure system ahead in our flight path.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:44.800
Just in case, please fasten your seatbelts.

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:06.880
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:15.290
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:26.380
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:35.900
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:44.930
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:50.440
I'll live feeling them

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:55.620
For me to be me

00:22:55.620 --> 00:23:04.080
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:09.720
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:19.450
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:31.240
To reunite with Jonouchi, Yugi and I returned to the train tracks.

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:36.700
Meanwhile, Kaiba flies to Florida to get the archaeological documents.

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:40.220
But Doma won't stand idly by!

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:44.290
Amelda infiltrates the plane for a rematch against Kaiba.

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:46.590
This time, it's a battle in the sky?

00:23:46.590 --> 00:23:50.440
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Amelda's Revenge
Duel in the Sky

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:52.080
Duel, standby!
